# Execution Timestamps

## When to Include Timestamps

Include a `[HH:MM:SS]` timestamp prefix in your chat response **at every meaningful phase boundary** during:

- Any deployment or Railway CLI operation
- Any CI / GitHub Actions polling loop
- Any multi-step test run (`npm run build`, `npm run test:*`)
- Any operation expected to take >10 seconds
- Any "waiting for..." status update
- The start and end of every agent session checklist

## Format

Use 12-hour time with AM/PM inline with the action summary:

```
[4:32:07 PM] Starting deploy to dev — merging PR #42...
[4:32:51 PM] Deploy workflow run is up — watch in Actions: https://github.com/.../runs/<id>
[4:45:02 PM] ✅ Deploy receipt — workflow succeeded; health: 200 OK.
```

## How to Get the Current Time

```bash
date +"%l:%M:%S %p" | sed 's/^ //'
```

## What NOT to Timestamp

- Single-file reads or edits
- Lint passes that complete in <3 seconds
- Conversational replies with no execution happening
